---
// Brief to blueprint generator, cloned into the home page by the script.
---
<template id="bp-tpl">
<section class="sec alt bpgen" id="bpgen"><div class="wrap">
  <div class="head bpu"><span class="eyebrow">Brief to blueprint</span><h2>Describe the problem. Get a first-draft plan in ten seconds.</h2><p class="lead">Tell Yardie what isn't working. It briefs its agents and sketches an indicative plan right here in your browser. Nothing is sent unless you choose to send it.</p></div>
  <div class="bpg bpu">
    <div class="card">
      <label for="bpt">What's not working?</label>
      <textarea id="bpt" rows="5" placeholder="For example: our checkout slows down on sale days and support is drowning in tickets."></textarea>
      <div class="bpsig" id="bpsig" aria-live="polite"><span class="bps0">Topics Yardie spots will appear here</span></div>
      <div class="bpex"><span>Try:</span>
        <button type="button" data-ex="Our checkout slows down and our servers go down on sale days.">Slow on sale days</button>
        <button type="button" data-ex="We need an AI assistant to answer customer support questions.">AI for support</button>
        <button type="button" data-ex="Nine spreadsheets run our reporting and nobody trusts the numbers.">Spreadsheet chaos</button>
        <button type="button" data-ex="Our old mainframe system must be modernised and pass a security audit.">Legacy plus audit</button>
        <button type="button" data-ex="Our hotel's housekeeping runs on WhatsApp and radios, and rooms are late for early arrivals.">Hotel housekeeping chaos</button>
        <button type="button" data-ex="Our website has to work with screen readers and keyboards before an accessibility audit in March.">Accessibility deadline</button>
      </div>
      <span class="err" id="bperr"></span>
      <button class="btn pri" id="bpgo" type="button"><span>Draw my blueprint</span><span class="arrow">&rarr;</span></button>
    </div>
    <div class="card bpplan" id="bpplan"></div>
  </div>
</div></section>
</template>
